    "proof": "Hash equality proves equal declared descriptors, not accurate graph, compiler truth, build consumption or signed provenance",
    "capture": "every digest has one explicit actual file/collection binding; consume private immutable snapshots, not original paths; completeness and actual build consumption require separate evidence",
    "embedding": "explicit schema2 emitter/parser only; schema1 entrypoints remain strict; no descriptor path fallback",
    "circularity": "engine, bridge, fallback and link identities refer to pre-embedding inputs; never include the final identity-bearing source/binary hash back into its own descriptor; final signed binary is bound by separate build attestation",
    "release": "signed verified grants only narrow installed sets and base resource limits; no native implementation/path/startup/effects-gate selector",
    "definition": "This descriptor confers no authority without implementing installed factory and verified selection; status and qualification are external to its byte-hashed definition"
